lity so an own root is a trusted boundary only on independently established prior ancestry/attribution evidence; the candidate/current staging operation cannot qualify merely by being recorded or live. Define which previously checked own roots may stop, how their evidence is retained, and how the starting commit is treated. Retain historical inputs consistent with the separate ancestry replay finding in fb0d5867. A compact witness with D/U/I should visit U and either refuse unnamed-work or require its recorded selection/authors. No scope reduction or new runtime quota is needed.\n\nROOT reread whole1491-1505,1540-1618,1620-1855 and relevant R2 prerequisites. An independent static reader separately confirmed the witness and the live-transition ambiguity. Full prior document coverage and exact six-file manifest remain in fb0d5867; this supplements it, not a new full-source or measured claim. Confidence high, design-contract finding. No execution, test, private diagnostic, source edit, provider effect or reviewer/model restart.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true"}}